  'prior-attempts-http-smoke.js', // WHAT WAS ALREADY TRIED, AND WHY THE ANSWER CHANGES WHEN AN OUTCOME IS RECORDED. Acceptance matrix 12-14. THE DEFECT WAS A LAYER THAT ONLY EXISTS WHEN A MODEL IS WRITING: ai/composer.js carries prior attempts into the model's context and its system prompt already forbids repackaging a materially identical unsuccessful one, but a turn bound to a group focus makes ONE provider call -- the bounded action read -- and the prose comes from the deterministic object reader, so with models off (the pilot's state) none of it reached anybody. A coach on their second attempt asking what else to try was told what they were working on and that nothing had been recorded about it, while the record held that the first attempt had been tried and had not helped: the most useful fact available was the one left out. AND THE RELATIONSHIP HAS TWO SPELLINGS -- a personal focus stores `addresses:{kind,id}`, a group focus stores `origin.inquiryId` -- so the reader knew about a personal focus's question and not a group's; read under both names here rather than renamed, because consolidating them is a canonical-owner change with its own blast radius and this is a reader. A is the control (nothing tried, nothing claimed to have been); B proves the reply changes once an outcome exists, carries the recorded outcome word, keeps the causal limitation on the qa the reader receives, and still proposes no tactic of its own; C proves it is scoped to the recorded relationship rather than to resemblance, so an attempt on a different question does not bleed across; D proves a SUCCESSFUL attempt is reported as precedent that still carries the causal limitation rather than as proof the tactic works.
  'forum-ask-http-smoke.js', // ASK INTELLIQ INSIDE A FORUM, WITHOUT SPEAKING IN IT. FOUNDER RULING, September 2026, after this seam was escalated rather than built: answer the asker privately using only the Forum/object-governed projection; never automatically publish that answer to the room; sharing must remain deliberate through the existing governed share path. WHY IT WAS ESCALATED: Priority R&D P2 asks that any governed Forum expose Ask IntelliQ, and that is not a UI task -- every other assistant answer is built from _allObjectsFor(code,userId), the individual reader's whole authorised set, which is WIDER than the room and DIFFERS between two people in it, so answering from that set and letting the answer reach the room would widen readership by exactly the gap between them. The ruling removes the problem rather than solving it: the scope is the OBJECT and the answer never reaches the room on its own. The three properties this file exists for are therefore PRIVACY properties rather than answer quality -- the room's own live gate decides who may ask (a non-member is refused exactly as the room refuses them); the answer is bounded to the object's projection, proved by TWO different members of one room receiving the SAME answer (if it were built per-reader the two would diverge, and that difference is precisely what would leak if either reached the room); and nothing is posted -- no message, no author, no timestamp, the room byte-for-byte unchanged, another member opening it a moment later seeing none of it, and the payload saying `posted:false` rather than leaving a client to infer it from an absence. D pins that the route writes no message and persists nothing, and that the deliberate share path still reaches the room, so this did not close a door while opening one. DETERMINISTIC: models are off, which is the pilot's state, and the answer is composed by the route -- this pass established that a rule living only in a model prompt is not implemented.
