  'group-subject-smoke.js', // GROUP AS A SUBJECT + THE CONTRIBUTION BOUNDARY (HTTP, model OFF): group:<nodeId> is a subjectRef like member:<userId> and everything downstream — identity, hypotheses, confidence, origin, corrections, frontier — is the machinery Self already uses; the kernel contains no group branch at all, which this asserts against the source. What is new is the boundary in FRONT of it, because membership is not consent: a member belonging to U18 must never mean everything they say becomes U18 evidence. Pins that relevance and authorisation are asked SEPARATELY (a model claiming group relevance without collective language in the person's own words is declined; an interpretation can never carry it, since those are our words not theirs); that a candidate is private to whoever produced it and invisible to teammates AND to the node leader; that nothing is ever contributed automatically and a leader may not publish a member's account for them; that the opening rule counts INDEPENDENT ORIGINS not voices, so three people repeating one origin is named as an ECHO and opens nothing while two genuine origins do; that contribution mints no new independence and a retelling stays a retelling; that a contributor can withdraw and the group evidence is superseded rather than deleted, with history intact; that no verbatim private span, unrelated Self inquiry, safeguarding excerpt or other org's data can reach a group read; and an eight-step end-to-end squad scenario from "I get nervous before matches" (Self, no candidate) through corroboration, an authoritative coach account, hearsay and a self-correction.
