  'pilot-crackdown-smoke.js',       // WHAT A REAL PERSON HIT ON A REAL PHONE. Each assertion pins one live defect shut: an ordinary QUESTION about an object being turned into a Focus titled with the question (seven of them were, in every context); Settings rendering "1 undefined" because the seed wrote bare strings into a store whose routes look up metricId, which also made every seeded metric silently unrenamable and undeletable; an audience chip printing a bare reach count glued to the group name, so a coach read "Alma College Men's Soccer1"; native browser prompts for naming a Library folder and correcting a proposal; and an invite card offering to "send personalised email invites" when nothing in the repository sends email. Also guards the persistence shape that the transfer bill depends on -- split by default, units not blobs, and a save that costs what it changed
